21],[-123.11129,49.27214],[-123.11105,49.27212],[-123.11103,49.27205],[-123.11093,49.27202],[-123.11056,49.27214],[-123.11039,49.27213],[-123.11009,49.27235],[-123.11018,49.27241],[-123.11065,49.27244],[-123.11118,49.2723],[-123.11136,49.27221]]]]},"wikidata":"Q24639","facts":{"population":{"value":662248,"year":2021},"founded":{"year":1886,"label":"1886"},"elevation":2,"officialArea":115,"website":"https://vancouver.ca/","mayor":"Ken Sim"},"summary":{"extract":"Vancouver is a major city in Western Canada, located in the Lower Mainland region of British Columbia. As the most populous city in the province, the 2021 Canadian census recorded 662,248 people in the city, up from 631,486 in 2016. The Greater Vancouver area had a population of 2.6 million in 2021, making it the third-largest metropolitan area in Canada after Toronto and Montreal. The region, together with the Fraser Valley, makes up the Lower Mainland, which has a total population of over 3 million. Vancouver has the highest population density in Canada, with over 5,700 inhabitants per square kilometre (15,000/sq mi), and the fourth highest in North America.","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Skyline_of_Vancouver%2C_Canada.jpg/330px-Skyline_of_Vancouver%2C_Canada.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vancouver"},"twins":["Q38283","Q1874","Q23436","Q16572","Q65","Q8678","Q9899","Q51103","Q159273","Q612"],"climate":{"temp":[3.1,3.1,5.3,8.6,13.8,16.9,20.1,20.1,16.6,11.2,6,2.6],"rain":[323,165,253,145,96,84,50,61,122,233,348,295],"cloud":[81,75,81,78,71,71,50,50,58,73,81,81]},"land":true}